{"cluster_id": "C-3998", "topic": "CAS disk command names", "target": "operations/migration", "member_ids": ["B048-055", "B048-056"], "canonical_claim": "The user-facing disk commands are `cas-fsck`, `cas-gc-dryrun`, `cas-gc-rebuild`, `cas-inspect`, and `cas-drop-member`; the deprecated `fsck` alias and `CommandFsckDeprecated` factory and registration were removed, while C++ class names such as `CommandCaInspect` were retained. `clickhouse disks --query 'help'` lists the five `cas-*` commands and no `fsck`; querying `fsck` exits 36 and prints the available-command listing.", "issue_ids": ["T7"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t7-report.md#L17-L28", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t7-report.md#L29-L40"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3999", "topic": "The temporary-hard-link `BACKUP` path is rejected for CAS with a fail-cl", "target": "operations/migration", "member_ids": ["B051-082"], "canonical_claim": "The temporary-hard-link `BACKUP` path is rejected for CAS with a fail-closed exception because it clones files through a non-part temporary path; Atomic and UUID databases use the pointer-holding path that round-trips.", "issue_ids": ["B34"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#data-part-storage-on-disk-base"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4000", "topic": "`MergeTreeData::restorePartFromBackup` uses a `restore_tx` whole-part tr", "target": "operations/migration", "member_ids": ["B035-095", "B051-095"], "canonical_claim": "`MergeTreeData::restorePartFromBackup` uses a `restore_tx` whole-part transaction for atomic restore, mirroring `freeze`.; The coverage audit considers the backup/restore source a thin RESTORE bug-fix specification rather than architecture: `BACKUP` read-side works, while `RESTORE` must materialize each part through one whole-part commit rather than per-file autocommit.", "issue_ids": ["B198"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#second-pass-pass", "docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#merge-tree-data-cpp"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4001", "topic": "The classic `clickhouse-backup` (Altinity) freeze-and-copy mode is incom", "target": "operations/migration", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-064"], "canonical_claim": "The classic `clickhouse-backup` (Altinity) freeze-and-copy mode is incompatible with CAS because there are no local metadata files and no filesystem shadow (shadow lives in-pool as refs); only its embedded mode, which wraps native `BACKUP`, applies.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/10-backups.md#clickhouse-backup"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4002", "topic": "Logical export (Iceberg/Parquet/datalake) is the ultimate independence t", "target": "operations/migration", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-066"], "canonical_claim": "Logical export (Iceberg/Parquet/datalake) is the ultimate independence tier (readable without ClickHouse, directly queryable by other engines) but is lossy: `AggregateFunction` states do not survive Parquet, and `LowCardinality`, codecs, skip indexes, projections, and physical `ORDER BY` layout are all lost; restore is a full re-insert, the longest RTO in the survey.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/10-backups.md#logical-export"]}
